CONTEXT (full, self-contained): Bug report: a list of 20 items with pageSize=20 showed an extra empty page. Reproduction confirmed on revision 5f50ddb, systematic: any non-empty input got one extra empty page (20/20 → [20,0]; 25/20 → [20,5,0]; 10/20 → [10,0]; 0/20 → [[]] which is the intended contract per an existing test).

ROOT CAUSE (lead's claim, verify it): src/paginate.js computed pageCount as Math.floor(n/size) + (n%size ? 1 : 0) + (n>0 ? 1 : 0). The third term adds a phantom page to every non-empty input; at an exact multiple it duplicates the already-counted full page.

FIX APPLIED (full current content of src/paginate.js):
```js
export function paginate(items, pageSize = 10) {
  const pages = [];
  const pageCount = Math.ceil(items.length / pageSize);
  for (let i = 0; i < pageCount; i++) {
    pages.push(items.slice(i * pageSize, (i + 1) * pageSize));
  }
  if (pages.length === 0) pages.push([]);
  return pages;
}
```
